# Build-context exclusions, shared by Dockerfile (CI) and deploy/Dockerfile.jetson.
#
# tests/ is deliberately NOT excluded: the CI image's whole job is to run them, and
# the previous version of this file excluded them while the CI workflow claimed to
# test the image.
#
# models/*.onnx and models/*.engine are excluded because they are large and because
# an .engine is tied to the TensorRT build and GPU that produced it — baking one in
# produces an image that silently fails to deserialise on the next board. The Jetson
# compose profile bind-mounts ./models read-only instead.

# Version control and CI metadata
.git
.gitignore
.gitmodules
.github/

# Python build and cache artefacts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
*.egg-info/
src/adas_core.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Editors and OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Environments
.env
.venv/
venv/
ENV/

# Vendored upstream source (only needed to export the UFLD ONNX off-board)
Ultra-Fast-Lane-Detection-v2/

# Model artefacts: bind-mount them, never bake them in
models/*.onnx
models/*.pt
models/*.pth
models/*.engine
models/*.log

# Runtime output that must never be shipped inside an image
data/
recordings/
logs/
*.log
*.mp4
*.avi
*.jsonl

# Documentation the images do not need (README.md is kept: pyproject references it)
docs/
*.md
!README.md
